From: Lokbondo Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:12:09 -0700
Subject: [vulkan] Reset the recording context in Queue::DestroyImpl.

- Prior to this change, Queue::DestroyImpl freed the current recording
  context's command pool and buffer, but left the dangling handles in
  mRecordingContext. If the recording context was used after the
  device was destroyed (e.g. by SharedTextureMemory::EndAccess
  performing an export transition submit), commands would be recorded
  into a freed VkCommandBuffer, causing a heap use-after-free in the
  driver.
- This change resets mRecordingContext after freeing its resources so
  that no dangling handles survive destruction. Any later use of the
  recording context sees null handles instead of freed objects.

Bug: 577377985
Change-Id: I5440510d199218309d2da4ef9fcdf50529610fe9
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/354676
Commit-Queue: Loko Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

diff --git a/src/dawn/native/vulkan/QueueVk.cpp b/src/dawn/native/vulkan/QueueVk.cpp
index 1624a69e2328f598e48e73c3ea18785c23350a5a..cd2f1e952e456a1f62c5d1c5a48bc94991942a10 100644
--- a/src/dawn/native/vulkan/QueueVk.cpp
+++ b/src/dawn/native/vulkan/QueueVk.cpp
@@ -442,8 +442,10 @@ void Queue::DestroyImpl(DestroyReason reason) {
     for (VkSemaphore semaphore : mRecordingContext.waitSemaphores) {
         device->fn.DestroySemaphore(vkDevice, semaphore, nullptr);
     }
-    mRecordingContext.waitSemaphores.clear();
-    mRecordingContext.signalSemaphores.clear();
+    // Reset the recording context so that no dangling handles to the freed command pool/buffer
+    // survive destruction. Any later attempt to use the recording context then sees null handles
+    // instead of using freed objects.
+    mRecordingContext = CommandRecordingContext();
 
     // Free any recycled command pools.
     mUnusedCommands.Use([&](auto unusedCommands) {
